The changes:

- **Single type lookup.** `GetType()` was called up to twice. It is now called once, and the masked index is reused.
- **Direct buffer access.** The bytes are read through `values.data()`, which removes repeated `operator[]` indexing.
- **`memcpy` fast path.** When the base-type size equals `sizeof(T)`, the buffer holds 1-byte elements, and the build is little-endian, the value is loaded with one `memcpy`. On little-endian machines this produces the same value as the shift loop.
- **Unchanged fallback.** Every other case runs the original shift loop, so results and out-of-range behavior stay identical.

```cpp
template <typename T>
T FieldBase::GetValue(const FIT_UINT8 fieldArrayIndex) const
{
    const FIT_UINT8 typeNum = GetType() & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK;
    const FIT_UINT8 size = baseTypeSizes[typeNum];
    if (fieldArrayIndex >= (FIT_UINT8)values.size())
    {
        return *reinterpret_cast<const T*>(baseTypeInvalids[typeNum]);
    }

    const auto* p = values.data() + (fieldArrayIndex * size);

#if defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) && defined(__ORDER_LITTLE_ENDIAN__) && (__BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_LITTLE_ENDIAN__)
    if ((size == sizeof(T)) && (sizeof(*p) == 1))
    {
        T rv;
        std::memcpy(&rv, p, sizeof(T));
        return rv;
    }
#endif

    T rv = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++)
    {
        rv |= static_cast<T>(p[i]) << (i * 8);
    }

    return rv;
}
```

